{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0113qKyP5YiQ3tHCKvhvDkUw","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The final decision is to **remove the `group.protocol` client configuration entirely in Kafka 6.0**.  \\\\n\\\\n- 2026-01-27T02:46:33.000000Z - `mail:8379690aa2bf96c5b418ae3e` - discussion about keeping `group.protocol=consumer` and not removing the config entirely.  \\\\n- 2026-01-28T09:50:37.000000Z - `mail:263b0239b98e36fe0c99fba8` - Andrew Schofield comments that removing the config would be unnecessary and suggests keeping it with a single value.  \\\\n- 2026-01-28T12:49:28.000000Z - `mail:c64a83d2563f7ab1569d318f` - Lianet Magrans states the group.protocol config will be kept but validated to only support `consumer`.  \\\\n- 2026-01-28T16:53:06.000000Z - `mail:2034d686308bfb1f60b2770e` - Matthias J. Sax advocates removal of the config in 6.0, noting it will be deprecated in 5.0 and then deleted.  \\\\n- 2026-01-28T??:??:??.000000Z - `mail:745ef36c7a7bc568bde226af` - KIP-1274 accepted, confirming the plan to deprecate and remove the config.  \\\\n- 2026-01-28T??:??:??.000000Z - `mail:e437a5f929aa48c75a64ae98` - Lianet Magrans clarifies that the intention is to deprecate the public-facing `group.protocol` config in 5.0 and remove it in 6.0.  \\\\n\\\\nThe later, more recent messages (especially `mail:2034d686308bfb1f60b2770e`, `mail:745ef36c7a7bc568bde226af`, and `mail:e437a5f929aa48c75a64ae98`) establish the final stance: the configuration will be deleted in Kafka 6.0.  \\\\n\\\\nNo other records contradict this final decision.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:2034d686308bfb1f60b2770e\\\",\\\"mail:263b0239b98e36fe0c99fba8\\\",\\\"mail:627e735177597c7ef8fa2243\\\",\\\"mail:8379690aa2bf96c5b418ae3e\\\",\\\"mail:c64a83d2563f7ab1569d318f\\\",\\\"mail:745ef36c7a7bc568bde226af\\\",\\\"mail:e437a5f929aa48c75a64ae98\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":34.36,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":23,\\\"usage\